          "The sigmatic pattern does not make every stem predictable from its present form. καίω, “burn,” forms ἔκαυσα; κλαίω, “weep,” forms ἔκλαυσα. Their αυ before σ must be learned with the principal parts, rather than generated by retaining the present -αι-.",
