  "wordStudy": {
    "label": "Word Study — πόνος is not the whole story",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "title": "πόνος is not the whole story",
        "practiceTopic": "word-study",
        "body": [
          "πόνος can mean toil, exertion, or hardship. καρτερία names endurance. Their association in moral writing does not mean that more suffering always produces more virtue.",
          "Add βοήθεια, “help,” to the pair. This episode asks who makes continued movement possible. A vocabulary list can become a map of relationships, not merely a set of private qualities."
        ],
        "display": [
          {
            "greek": "ὁ πόνος",
            "english": "toil, hardship"
          },
          {
            "greek": "ἡ καρτερία",
            "english": "endurance"
          },
          {
            "greek": "ἡ βοήθεια",
            "english": "help"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
