        "title": "1. Athematic second aorists",
        "practiceTopic": "root-aorists",
        "body": [
          "Some second aorists attach endings directly to a root, without a thematic ο/ε vowel. Recognize ἔβην from βαίνω and ἔστην from ἵστημι. Like other aorist indicatives, they carry an augment and present a past event as a whole.",
          "Their meaning must be learned with their principal parts. ἔβην means “I went/stepped”; ἔστην means “I stood,” not “I made someone stand.” The full transitive contrast returns in Lesson 35."
        ],
