        "title": "2. Aorist infinitives, participles, commands",
        "practiceTopic": "root-nonfinite",
        "body": [
          "Outside the indicative, the aorist does not take an augment. βῆναι is an infinitive; βάς is a masculine nominative singular participle. Its feminine is βᾶσα, neuter βάν. The genitive βάντος reveals the -ντ- stem.",
          "Aorist commands present the requested action as a whole: βῆθι, “go!” Compare στῆθι, “stand!” Aorist participles normally show action prior to the main verb, though context determines the precise relation."
        ],
