        "id": "further-es",
        "title": "3. Recognizing -εσ- nouns in difficult terrain",
        "practiceTopic": "further-es",
        "body": [
          "Apply the -εσ- noun pattern to the physical world: τὸ ὄρος, τοῦ ὄρους, “mountain”; τὸ βάθος, τοῦ βάθους, “depth.” τὸ χεῖλος, τοῦ χείλους can mean a lip or an edge. The genitive -ους comes from contraction, not second declension.",
          "Nominative and accusative neuter forms coincide. τὰ ὄρη can therefore be a subject or object; context decides. After ἐν, τοῖς ὄρεσιν is dative plural."
        ],
