        "3. ἐπίσταμαι: knowing how: ἐπίσταμαι means “know, understand,” including knowing how to perform a task. With an infinitive it expresses practical knowledge: ἐπίσταται κομίζειν, “she knows how to carry.” This is different from δύναται, which emphasizes capacity or opportunity.",
        "4. Matching verb and complement: An infinitive can complete an idea left unfinished by a verb: “can ...,” “knows how ...,” “wishes ...”. In ordinary same-subject examples, the subject of the infinitive is the subject of the finite verb."
