        "title": "1. δίδωμι in the present and imperfect",
        "practiceTopic": "didomi-present",
        "body": [
          "δίδωμι is athematic: its endings attach to the stem without the ordinary thematic ο/ε. The present singular has a long vowel, δίδωμι, δίδως, δίδωσι; the plural has short ο, δίδομεν, δίδοτε, διδόασι.",
          "The imperfect is irregular in the singular: ἐδίδουν, ἐδίδους, ἐδίδου; plural ἐδίδομεν, ἐδίδοτε, ἐδίδοσαν. A gift commonly has a recipient in the dative and an object in the accusative."
        ],
